  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="meta">
    Jean Social Artist Autopilot (JSAA)<br>
    Effective date: 11 November 2026
  </div>

  <p>
    Jean Social Artist Autopilot ("JSAA") is a creator tool designed to help an artist
    prepare, review and manage short-form music content for social platforms such as TikTok
    and Instagram.
  </p>

  <p>
    JSAA is currently operated as a local, single-user application. The main application,
    media files, project database and generated content are stored on the user's own computer
    unless the user explicitly chooses to send content to an external service.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information JSAA may process</h2>
  <p>Depending on the features used, JSAA may process:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Basic social account information, such as display name, username or account identifier.</li>
    <li>OAuth authorization data and access tokens required to connect a supported social platform.</li>
    <li>Music, lyrics, artwork, captions, hashtags, images and videos supplied by the user.</li>
    <li>User-created preferences, approvals, rejections and editing choices used to improve the local workflow.</li>
    <li>Technical information necessary to operate the application and its integrations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. TikTok data</h2>
  <p>
    If the user connects a TikTok account, JSAA may request only the permissions needed for
    the enabled TikTok features.
  </p>
  <p>
    Basic TikTok account information may be used to identify and display the account connected
    to JSAA. If TikTok content-upload functionality is enabled in the future, JSAA may use the
    relevant TikTok permission to transfer a user-approved video to the user's TikTok account.
  </p>
  <p>
    JSAA does not automatically publish content without user action. Content preparation,
    approval and publishing remain under the user's control.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Use of AI services</h2>
  <p>
    JSAA may use external AI services, including OpenAI APIs, when the user requests functions
    such as concept generation, text generation, semantic analysis or image generation.
    Only information required to perform the requested operation is sent to the relevant service.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How information is used</h2>
  <p>Information processed by JSAA is used only to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide the requested content-creation and preparation features.</li>
    <li>Connect the user's own social accounts when explicitly authorized.</li>
    <li>Generate and render user-requested content.</li>
    <li>Remember user-approved creative preferences within the JSAA application.</li>
    <li>Prepare content for manual or authorized platform publishing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Data sharing</h2>
  <p>JSAA does not sell personal data.</p>
  <p>
    Information may be transmitted to external services only when necessary to perform a
    user-requested function, for example to OpenAI for AI generation or to TikTok for account
    authorization or an authorized upload operation.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data storage</h2>
  <p>
    JSAA is designed primarily as a local application. Application data, media, generated files
    and preferences are normally stored on the user's own system.
  </p>
  <p>
    Authentication tokens for connected services are intended to be stored by the backend
    application and are not exposed in the public frontend.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    The user controls locally stored JSAA data. Songs, generated content, project records and
    connected-account information may be removed from the local application by the user.
  </p>
  <p>
    The user may also revoke JSAA's access to a connected social account through the relevant
    platform's account or authorization settings.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>JSAA is not designed or intended for use by children.</p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    JSAA is designed to keep private application data and credentials out of the public website
    and public source repositories. Sensitive credentials such as API keys, client secrets and
    access tokens should remain in the local backend environment and must not be published.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy may be updated as JSAA functionality changes or as new platform
    integrations are added. The effective date above will be updated when material changes
    are made.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions regarding this Privacy Policy can be submitted through the JSAA project owner.
  </p>

  <footer>
    Jean Social Artist Autopilot (JSAA)
  </footer>

